WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.580
Breathing, digestion and fertility
belong to three separate body systems.

2
00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:09.460
In cystic fibrosis, all
three can be affected.

3
00:00:09.510 --> 00:00:14.200
Yet the cause lies in a
single gene, called CFTR.

4
00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:18.020
Over 2000 different variants
of it have been recorded.

5
00:00:18.070 --> 00:00:22.270
So how can one faulty protein in
cell membranes affect breathing,

6
00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:24.810
digestion and fertility?

7
00:00:24.860 --> 00:00:28.130
In this mission, you'll meet
the protein that gene makes,

8
00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:31.710
sitting in the membranes of the
cells that line your airways.

9
00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:36.460
Then you'll read results from the sweat
test used to diagnose the condition.

10
00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:41.540
Your mission: explain how one faulty
membrane protein can affect breathing,

11
00:00:41.590 --> 00:00:43.470
digestion and fertility.
